## 4. Pages mein kaise add karein

1. Publish approved platform content at public HTTPS routes such as `/privacy` and `/terms`. Link both from the website footer and signup or onboarding. Put Terms acceptance beside the signup action. Show a separate optional marketing choice where used.
2. Each tenant should use its own customer-facing privacy notice where it controls collection. The existing widget reads `privacyPolicyUrl`, `termsUrl` and `grievanceEmail` from its theme configuration. Set and verify the actual three values for each tenant. Check the widget footer, menu and final form screen. Existing branches can fall back to different hard-coded platform domains. Standardize published destinations and check mobile and anonymous access. [Theme DTO](../src/main/java/com/chatcrmlite/backend/dto/ThemeConfigDTO.java) · [Theme service](../src/main/java/com/chatcrmlite/backend/services/NicheThemeService.java) · [Widget UI](../src/main/resources/static/widget/ui.js)
3. At the point of collection, add a short purpose-specific notice before form submission, recording or activating optional tracking. Example for an enquiry: “We use the details you provide to respond to your enquiry. See [Business Privacy Policy].” Keep marketing an optional, unchecked choice. Confirm a simple way to withdraw it on each channel.
4. Track Terms acceptance, privacy notice version and purpose-specific consent as separate server-side events where relevant. Onboarding currently stores a consent timestamp. Some widget paths set consent based on a name or email or send a hard-coded version. Capture the actual choice, version, purpose, time and channel and test withdrawal and enforcement. [Onboarding](../src/main/java/com/chatcrmlite/backend/controllers/OnboardingController.java) · [Widget flow engine](../src/main/resources/static/widget/flow-engine.js)
5. Verify erasure before writing retention promises. The WebChat service deletes messages and their selected chat session. Lead, contact, support, archive, vendor and backup data require their own checks. The existing database job archives selected records after 90 days. Remove the widget's broad “DPDP Compliant” badge and align erasure copy with the verified behavior before release. [WebChat service](../src/main/java/com/chatcrmlite/backend/services/WebChatService.java) · [Retention job](../src/main/java/com/chatcrmlite/backend/services/DatabaseRetentionService.java)
6. Set the verified Privacy Policy URL in the Google OAuth configuration if the app is public. Verify each scope's use and Google's Limited Use requirements before publishing the corresponding statement. [Google API Services User Data Policy](https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy) · [Google Workspace user data policy](https://developers.google.com/workspace/workspace-api-user-data-developer-policy)
7. Before publishing, confirm legal entity, privacy and grievance contacts, real production vendors and regions, actual retention schedule, Google data practices, subscription and refund rules, and the frontend cookie inventory. Test the final links and the privacy request workflow end to end.

## Reference points

- India DPDP core obligations are subject to the notified phase-in. Review the current enforcement timeline and rules before publishing. [MeitY commencement notification](https://www.meity.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/11/c56ceae6c383460ca69577428d36828b.pdf)
- For applicable GDPR processing, review territorial scope, transparency, lawful grounds, rights, processor terms and international transfers. [Official GDPR text](https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2016/679)
